Build a solid classifier's face intersectors in parallel

Targets OCCT V8_0_1. Introduced in Fillet on 2026-10-26 (e99c150).

BRepClass3d_SolidExplorer::InitShape builds an IntCurvesFace_Intersector
(a sampled polyhedron for B-spline faces) for every face of the solid, one
after another, before any point is classified. On the benchmark fixture that
was about 20% of a cold evaluate: BOPAlgo_BuilderSolid classifying the result
shells of every boolean (on the calling thread, while OCCT's pool sits idle)
and finish()'s inside-out check.

The patch builds the intersectors on OCCT's thread pool (OSD_Parallel::For)
and binds them in face order afterwards. Each intersector depends only on its
face, so the explorer ends up exactly as before: a face that occurs twice is
still bound last-wins (the replaced intersector is deleted instead of leaked),
and if a face throws, the faces before it are bound and the first exception in
face order is rethrown. Cold evaluate about 2 200 -> 1 900 ms; finish()'s
orientation check 208 -> 83 ms.

